      "text": "card: where the host draws Keel cards, the user sees what follows as a card carrying its name, links and ids, so a reply can call it by name; the ids and links here serve tool calls and hosts without cards.\n\nMap a strategy's settings · Lookback × hold · version 1 · Done · Oct 29\nNearby settings as a share of yours: −0.78 (nearby −0.23 against yours 0.29)\nDays Mar 23, 2025 to Oct 29, 2026, split Apr 17, 2026 · 100 coins: the coins Momentum rotation trades · costs 9 bp a fill · data as of Oct 29, 2026\nIn short:\n- Nearby settings as a share of yours: −0.78 (nearby −0.23 against yours 0.29), no interval; Mar 23, 2025 to Oct 28, 2026\n- Rank among nearby settings: 3 of 9, no interval; Mar 23, 2025 to Oct 28, 2026\n- Rank agreement before and after the split: 0.041, no interval (No range shown: these numbers use the same days); Mar 23, 2025 to Oct 28, 2026\nBest settings (of 384): hold 30 · lookback 7: Sharpe 1.38; hold 6 · lookback 18: Sharpe 1.38; hold 5 · lookback 90: Sharpe 1.38; hold 14 · lookback 8: Sharpe 1.37; hold 7 · lookback 12: Sharpe 1.37\nRuns: 0 runs, 0 reused, none failed\nCharts (4): Lookback × hold · Before vs after the split · Every setting · Across holds. keel_research_get(study_id=\"stu_000005\", view=0) reads the numbers behind any of them.\nMeasured with nearby settings and before and after the split.\nMomentum rotation v3 has a newer version, v4. Plan it: keel_research_plan(study_id=\"stu_000005\", source=\"Study(\\n    title=\\\"Lookback × hold\\\",\\n    question=\\\"How do the results change around lookback 10, hold 28?\\\",\\n)\\n\\nSubjects(\\n    v3=Strategy(\\\"str_momrotpro00000000000000000@4\\\"),\\n)\\n\\nRun(\\n    days=Days(\\\"2025-03-23\\\", \\\"2026-10-29\\\"),\\n    split=Split(\\\"2026-04-17\\\"),\\n    coins=Coins([\\\"BTC\\\", \\\"ETH\\\", \\\"SOL\\\", \\\"HYPE\\\", \\\"XRP\\\", \\\"DOGE\\\", \\\"SUI\\\", \\\"BNB\\\", \\\"ADA\\\", \\\"LINK\\\", \\\"AVAX\\\", \\\"TRX\\\", \\\"LTC\\\", \\\"BCH\\\", \\\"DOT\\\",